{"tool_name":"rsat-retrieve-ensembl-seq","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"rsat-retrieve-ensembl-seq","home":"http://rsat.sb-roscoff.fr/retrieve-ensembl-seq_form.cgi","license":"AFL-3.0","summary":"Returns upstream, downstream, intronic, exonic, UTR, transcript, mRNA, CDS or gene sequences for a list of genes from the EnsEMBL database.\nMulti-genome queries are supported: automatic retrieval of sequences for all the orthologs of the query genes, at a given taxonomical level.","addition_date":"2019-12-13T13:39:03Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:27Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Web application","Web service"],"collections":["FR","Regulatory Sequence Analysis Tools (RSAT)","elixir-fr-sdp-2019"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:rsat-retrieve-ensembl-seq","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"gridid":"grid.4989.c","name":"Universit\u00e9 Libre de Bruxelles","typeEntity":"Institute","url":"https://www.ulb.be/"},{"name":"Morgane Thomas-Chollier","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2608-476X","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"name":"Olivier Sand","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1465-1640","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer","Documentor","Maintainer","Primary contact","Support"]}],"documentation":[{"note":"Documentation for the SOAP/WSDL Web services","type":["API documentation"],"url":"http://pedagogix-tagc.univ-mrs.fr/rsat/htmllink.cgi?title=RSAT%20:%20Web%20services%20documentation&file=web_services/RSATWS_documentation.xml"},{"type":["General"],"url":"https://rsat-doc.github.io/using-RSAT/"},{"type":["Installation instructions"],"url":"https://rsa-tools.github.io/installing-RSAT/"},{"type":["Training material"],"url":"https://teaching.rsat.eu/tutorials/tut_retrieve-ensembl-seq.html"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://teaching.rsat.eu/help.retrieve-ensembl-seq.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Identifier","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0842"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Data retrieval","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2422"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence set (nucleic acid)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1234"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"RSAT retrieve-ensembl-seq","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"olisand","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btp519","metadata":{"abstract":"The preparation of an appropriate sequence dataset is the starting point of all genomic analyses. We present retrieve-ensembl-seq, an application that considerably eases the retrieval of sequences from the Ensembl database, via our user-friendly web site or web services. The user provides Ensembl identifiers or gene names, and the program returns corresponding upstream, downstream, intronic, exonic, UTR or whole gene sequences. retrieve-ensembl-seq also offers a multiple organism mode to retrieve sequences from homologous genes at any taxonomical level. And we introduce various original filters such as the masking of coding fragments and the avoidance of sequence redundancy for genes with multiple transcripts. retrieve-ensembl-seq is included in the software suite regulatory sequence analysis tools (RSAT), allowing instant submission of retrieved sequences to further analysis tools. \u00a9 The Author 2009. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.","authors":[{"name":"Sand O."},{"name":"Thomas-Chollier M."},{"name":"van Helden J."}],"citationCount":10,"date":"2009-10-20T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"Retrieve-ensembl-seq: User-friendly and large-scale retrieval of single or multi-genome sequences from Ensembl"},"pmid":"19720677","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene regulation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0204"},{"term":"Nucleic acid sites, features and